led.\n\ngitreins verdict abfe0118 (run 2026-11-17/abfe0118): tier1 PASS, tier2 FAIL — 3 of 4 criteria verified on real npm 12.2.2 (allowScripts honoured; :memory: SELECT 1 probe; README/CHANGELOG remedy; gate red-proven by hiding better_sqlite3.node). Missing: the CI step, removed in e8343f1c and preserved as .coding-hermes/pending/ci-sqlite-binding-step.patch. Also flagged: the printed 'install-scripts approve' remedy was only dry-run verified — follow-up DF-SPECLANG-019.","id":"DF-SPECLANG-7","priority":"P2","reasoning":"Dogfood 2026-11-16, fresh clone (HEAD 2ace9a06), node v22.22.3 / npm 12.2.2, plain `npm install --no-audit --no-fund`. npm warns: \"1 package had install scripts blocked because they are not covered by allowScripts: better-sqlite3@12.11.1 (install: prebuild-install || node-gyp rebuild --release)\". After install there is no build/Release and no prebuilds/ under node_modules/better-sqlite3, and `new (require('better-sqlite3'))(':memory:')` fails with \"Could not locate the bindings file\" (require alone succeeds, so lint/tests that never open a DB do not catch it). package.json declares better-sqlite3 but carries no allowScripts/trustedDependencies, .npmrc is absent, and neither README nor GETTING-STARTED mentions the npm 12 remedy, so a fresh contributor silently gets a dead DB layer (dist/src/db/index.js:12 and the ralph-loop controller path). Note the bunker install leg runs `npm ci --ignore-scripts`, so the clean-machine fresh-install cell cannot see this class at all.","status":"in_progress","title":"P2 — fresh `npm install` on npm >=12 leaves better-sqlite3 without its native binding: DB layer unusable, repo declares no allowScripts","type":"bug","worktree":"/home/kara/worktrees/SpecLang-DF-SPECLANG-7","branch":"wt/DF-SPECLANG-7","sessions":["foreman-2026-11-17-02-12-03"],"blocked_reason":"CI wiring blocked: .github/workflows/ci.yml cannot be pushed from this host (token scopes repo,gist,read:org — no workflow scope). Deliverable parts landed